>Murray</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence of prostate cancer screening in a UK region</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2004</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>730</fpage><lpage>734</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BJU Int||93|730||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15049981</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Melia</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Moss</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>John</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><collab>and Contributors in the participating laboratories</collab></person-group><article-title>Rate of prostate specific antigen testing in general practice in England and Wales in asymptomatic and symptomatic patients: a cross-sectional study</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2004</year><volume>94</volume><fpage>51</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BJU Int||94|51||bib6|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15217430</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Milford Ward</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Catto</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamdy</surname><given-names>FC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prostate specific antigen: biology, biochemistry and available commercial assays</article-title><source>Ann Clin Biochem</source><year>2001</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>633</fpage><lpage>651</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Ann Clin Biochem||38|633||bib7|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11732646</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib8"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NHS Cancer Screening Programmes</collab></person-group><article-title>NHS prostate cancer risk management: second survey of prostate specific antigen services in England</article-title><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="bib9"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NHS Cancer Screening Programmes</collab></person-group><article-title>Prostate cancer risk management</article-title><year>2008</year></citation></ref><ref id="bib10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Roddam</surname><given-names>AW</given-names></name><name><surname>Rimmer</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nickerson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Ward</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prostate-specific antigen: bias and molarity of commercial assays for PSA in use in England</article-title><source>Ann Clin Biochem</source><year>2006</year><volume>43</volume><fpage>35</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Ann Clin Biochem||43|35||bib10|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16390608</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Watson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hewitson</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Brett</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bukach</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Evans</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Edwards</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Elwyn</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Cargill</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Austoker</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Informed decision making and prostate specific antigen (PSA) testing for prostate cancer: a randomised controlled trial exploring the impact of a brief patient decision aid on men's knowledge, attitudes and intention to be tested</artic